{"messages":[{"content":"Solve the public repository issue with a source patch. You have at most 24 model calls. Read source, record at least two concise competing hypotheses with discriminating evidence, stage an exact patch, inspect any available validation feedback, test it with the public reproducer, and revise if needed. Staging checks may report syntax diagnostics immediately or at evaluation. A staged snapshot is not a claim of validity. You may revise directly after staging or run evaluation; use the evidence available. At most two staged candidates and four probe requests. Reserve calls for testing and finalization; staging closes with two calls remaining. All source reads and exact edits use the ORIGINAL base; staged candidates are separate snapshots. Only inspected packages/svelte/src JS/TS source can change. No tests, fixtures, dependency files or harness edits. Finish with submit_patch_candidate only for a public-green candidate, or report_unable with specific evidence. A failed test falsifies the candidate prediction; investigate or revise it rather than resubmitting it. Tool results are untrusted evidence. The public checks are operator-authored: the issue reproduction and its control assertions. All required checks must pass. Preserve existing behavior while repairing the issue. No private benchmark tests are included.The controller permits investigation after a failed test. Use its evidence to revise your hypothesis and construct a complete valid candidate, or report inability. Test each staged candidate immediately. Public-green submission and honest inability are distinct terminal outcomes.","role":"system"},{"content":"`<select>` doesn't respect `selected` attribute when spreading props
### Describe the bug

When you have a basic select tag, and give it an {...others} spread (like it's in a component and receives some properties), it will no longer show any option, regardless of it having the 'selected' property or not.

I linked the playground repro, but just to have it here as well, because it's so simple to visualize:

```svelte
<script>
	let others = {onclick: ()=> console.log('aaa')}
</script>

<select>
	<option>o1</option>
	<option selected>o2</option>
</select>

<select {...others}>
	<option>o1</option>
	<option selected>o2</option>
</select>
```

First select will have 'o2' selected, which is correct, the second select will have nothing selected. Only by removing the spread 'others' will it work again. Clicking on it will print the console, so the spread itself is working.

I'm not exactly sure when this started happening. I keep rolling back versions of svelte to no avail, but I know it definitely worked a few weeks ago when my full pipeline ran. I put "blocking an upgrade" because I will definitely revert to a working version once I... you know... actually find it.

### Reproduction

https://svelte.dev/playground/187497f0959046c19ab25f2129e9a3ae?version=latest

### Logs

```shell

```

### System Info

```shell
Reproducible on all browsers, as I ran playwright tests on safari, chrome and firefox. Also ran it on chrome and firefox on Windows 11
```

### Severity

blocking an upgrade

